{"name":"Silk Chiffon","hex":"#ccbfc7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"},{"term":"chiffon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns made of silk, polyester, or cotton.","Any purely ornamental accessory on a woman's dress, such as a bunch of ribbon, lace, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chiffon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chiffon (fabric)","blocks":[{"text":"Chiffon, from the French word chiffe which means \"cloth or rag\"; is a lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns. Crepe yarn tends to have a tighter twist than standard yarns. The twist in the crepe yarns puckers the fabric slightly in both directions after weaving, giving it some stretch and a slightly rough feel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Lillian_Gish_2.jpg/330px-Lillian_Gish_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiffon_(fabric)"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/500px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/1280px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/No8633No8638No8626No9651.png/500px-No8633No8638No8626No9651.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coat and skirt street suit of gray chiffon broadcloth with embroidery and lace decoration (1905)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANo8633No8638No8626No9651.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/120px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/250px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg/120px-1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1970s_Givenchy_cocktail_dress%2C_orange_printed_silk_chiffon_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Meye